    <DocumentationNarrative Id="source:cli:meta-mesh:app:command:add-step:narrative:example-example-meta-mesh-add-step-stdin:author-a-step-with-stdin-arguments" DocumentationSubjectId="source:cli:meta-mesh:app:command:add-step" PreviousNarrativeId="source:cli:meta-mesh:app:command:add-step:narrative:guidance:token-substitution">
      <Body>Use --arguments-stdin when the child command has quoting-heavy arguments. The step remains modeled, while the argument text stays exactly as the child CLI expects it.

```powershell
@'
render-site --workspace ..\SuiteWorkspace --out ..\Site
'@ | meta-mesh add-step --operation regenerate-public-docs --name render-site --executable meta-docs --arguments-stdin --working-directory .
```</Body>
      <Origin>Authored</Origin>
      <ReviewStatus>Current</ReviewStatus>
      <Slot>Example.example:meta-mesh:add-step-stdin</Slot>
      <Title>Author a step with stdin arguments</Title>
    </DocumentationNarrative>
    <DocumentationNarrative Id="source:cli:meta-mesh:app:command:add-step:narrative:guidance:token-substitution" DocumentationSubjectId="source:cli:meta-mesh:app:command:add-step" PreviousNarrativeId="source:cli:meta-mesh:app:command:add-step:narrative:summary:summary">
      <Body>Step arguments can use `{workspace:&lt;name&gt;.location}` and `{workspace:&lt;name&gt;.surface}`. `.location` expands to the resolved path for XML and C# workspaces, and to the connection environment variable name for SQL workspaces. `.surface` expands to `xml`, `csharp`, or `sql`. `{env:NAME}` requires `NAME` to be non-empty and passes the variable name to the child CLI without exposing its value. Use `--arguments-stdin` when child arguments contain quotes, SQL, or shell-sensitive text.</Body>
      <Origin>Authored</Origin>
      <ReviewStatus>Current</ReviewStatus>
      <Slot>Guidance</Slot>
      <Title>Token substitution</Title>
    </DocumentationNarrative>
