    <DocumentationNarrative Id="source:cli:meta-mesh:app:narrative:guide:working-with-metamesh" DocumentationSubjectId="source:cli:meta-mesh:app" PreviousNarrativeId="source:cli:meta-mesh:app:narrative:summary:summary">
      <Body>`meta-mesh` turns a repository workflow into a workspace. The mesh declares the workspaces an operation uses and the ordered executable steps that create, inspect, transform, deploy, or run them.

Each operation is independently named and scoped. Before a run, MetaMesh resolves workspace locations, environment-variable tokens, executable paths, permissions, and step arguments. The same plan can be inspected with `steps` or `validate`, then executed with `run --operation &lt;name&gt;`.

The result is a repeatable workflow surface that people and agents can inspect before starting processes.</Body>
